{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Configure /srv/drop on node1 as a shared writable directory.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The directory was created as root:root with mode 1777, and two distinct unprivileged users successfully created files in it. Final verification showed the required permissions and an empty, ready-to-use directory.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d0aed39c9ce44037","cmd-8925e990584149ac","cmd-a80a5a83ff4c4edd"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Prevent users from removing files owned by other users while allowing owners to remove their own files.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Cross-owner deletion was directly denied with “Operation not permitted” in both directions, while owners successfully removed their own files. The behavior was also reverified after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8925e990584149ac","cmd-19187e305cb04401"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before and after execution, node1 reported CentOS 10 and kernel 6.12.0-205.el10.x86_64. The solution used existing filesystem permissions and standard installed utilities; no package or kernel change appears in the command timeline, and package health remained clean.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4e0c1fbfde5e4317","cmd-f521e822f9bd410c","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Creating /srv/drop was the required retained change. Test files and temporary error logs were bounded verification artifacts and were removed. The persistent canary, reboot, and post-reboot test artifacts supported the mandatory restart protocol; all artifacts were cleaned, the directory finished empty, no failed services appeared, package health remained clean, and listening exposure was unchanged apart from process identifiers after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d0aed39c9ce44037","cmd-8925e990584149ac","cmd-31960ebd345a45d9","cmd-50f1e7a51c694828","cmd-19187e305cb04401","cmd-a80a5a83ff4c4edd","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete and coherent: node1 was healthy before restart, the restart was acknowledged, its boot ID changed from be303eb3-eeb6-4466-86f1-fd6406dd7dad to de13bc6d-6a1a-4566-a0bb-bba08f49472c, and system health, directory permissions, canary data, and sticky-directory behavior recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":[]}
